<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Vennicnii</h1><p class="st-meta">100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">People of north-west Ireland recorded by Ptolemy, near a headland he called Vennicnium in modern Donegal.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Vennicnii are known only from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geography-ptolemy">Ptolemy's Geography</a> of about 150, which places them on the north-western coast of Ireland, with a headland named Vennicnium Promontorium, usually identified with Bloody Foreland or another point on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-donegal">Donegal</a> coast. His Irish information came from earlier sailors' reports.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nothing is recorded of their rulers, settlements or customs. The rugged coastline and uplands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-donegal">Donegal</a> supported small farming and fishing communities, and later stone forts such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grianan-of-aileach">Grianan of Aileach</a> show the importance of hilltop centres in the region.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>No later source mentions the Vennicnii. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-donegal">Donegal</a> later became the territory of the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-neill">Uí Néill</a> dynasties, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-conaill">Cenél Conaill</a> and the rulers of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ailech">Kingdom of Ailech</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:61.69%;width:1.99%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>100 CE – 200 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> – <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Goidelic Celtic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vennicones</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=vennicnii" aria-label="Vennicnii on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4485 365 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Vennicnii lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4805 621h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M4805 621h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Ireland. <a href="/atlas?year=150&amp;focus=vennicnii">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

